-- title:
--   Boolean boundary estimates control bounded cut correlations
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality, let $S$ be a face-regularity state on $G^{j+1}$, and let $f$ be real-valued there. If every Boolean boundary cut has absolute residual correlation with $f$ at most $\varepsilon$, then every bounded cut-test family $u$ has $|S.\mathrm{faceCutCorrelation}(f,u)|\le\varepsilon$.
